    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • 2026 Paris Motor Show: Jeep Reveals Six-Model European Strategy for 2030, Renegade Is Set to Return\nNFL's Tennessee Titans and Infiniti Team Up for a Luxury Game-Day Experience at New Nissan Stadium\n10 photos\nPhoto: Infiniti\nBefore you ask, the 'New Nissan Stadium' is the future home of the Tennessee Titans, in Nashville, Tennessee. It cost approximately $2.1 billion and boasts a capacity of roughly 60,000. This is an enclosed, climate-controlled stadium, unlike the existing Nissan Stadium which opened back in 1999. The new arena will host not only NFL games but also concerts, major college sporting events, and yes, even a future Super Bowl.\nWhile the new stadium is scheduled to open in 2027, the Titans won't move in until the 2027 season kicks off, which means they might want to settle in some time during next summer.\nWhat about the Super Bowl? Well, Super Bowl LXIV will take place at the new Nissan Stadium on Sunday, February 10, 2030. Save the date.\nWhile there, visitors will be able to take in the so-called Infiniti Club, a new premium hospitality area within the stadium. It's located along the south sideline within the lower-level seating bowl, and can accommodate up to 3,000 guests, making it one of the largest hospitality areas in American sports .\nThe space will feature premium amenities such as lounge seating overlooking the field, bar access, and striking visual elements meant to create a luxury feeling. I'd say they did a good job, judging from these official renderings. And yes, they are renderings, as opposed to AI slop. It's something to appreciate nowadays.\n\"The INFINITI Club reflects our commitment to creating exceptional experiences, combining bold design, elevated hospitality and a premium environment that feels distinctly INFINITI,\" stated Eric Ledieu, vice president, INFINITI Americas\n\"Every detail was designed to create a destination that feels as special as the events taking place inside the stadium, giving guests a new way to experience the INFINITI brand.\"\nWhat's interesting is that the club's inventory for Titans home games in 2027 is already sold out. But tickets for concerts and other third-party events should become available to the general public going forward.\nPhoto: Infiniti \"The space will be true to the INFINITI brand, giving fans a premium, connected way to experience Titans football, while continuing to push the envelope of making the game-day experience even better,\" stated the team's VP of client services and hospitality, Stephanie Atkins.\nThe Titans are not off to a good start in their 2026 campaign. Their current record is 1-5, with three home losses and just one victory on the road - they beat the Colts on Sunday 26-20, but that's nothing to write home about. The Colts are having a poor season too. Coming up during Week 7, the Titans will take on the Browns at home, with Cleveland being one of the better teams this year, surprisingly. They currently lead the AFC North with a record of 4-2 after six games.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nInfiniti Nissan NFL tennessee titans football Sports\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Sergiu Tudose\nSergiu got to experience both American and European car \"scenes\" at an early age (his father drove a Ford Fiesta XR2 supermini in the 80s). After spending over 15 years at local and international auto publications, he's starting to appreciate comfort behind the wheel more than raw power and acceleration. Full profile\nUP NEXT Mercedes-Benz CTO Joerg Burzer Says Gasoline and Electric Mercedes-AMG C 63 Are in the Works",
